# Spec apps

## Layout

```text
apps/<name>/
  app.yaml | security.yaml | module.go
  keymap.yaml         # optional — listed under app.yaml keymap:
  views/*.page.tsx
  locale/*.po
  __types__/          # generated — do not edit
  models/…            # optional split specs + hooks
```

Mirror `apps/hellospec` for CQRS (`queries` / `commands`) and `docs/tutorial/app-anatomy.md`.

## Contract

- `app.yaml` is source of truth for models, menus, locales, security, keymap includes.
- With `queries`/`commands`, pages bind via dotted refs: `query="app.field"`, `command="app.field"`.
- Computed fields use `compute:` (expression or `hook`) or `related:`. They are not form input. `store: false` is filled on read. See hellospec `length`, `label`, `topicName`, `shout`, and `preview`.
- `one2many` `inverse` must be a `many2one` on the related model in this spec that points back. Indexes: btree keys may be `field:desc`; `include` and `where` are btree-only. `indexed: true` is `(org_id, column)`.
- Without CQRS, generic GraphQL CRUD still exists; prefer named CQRS for public APIs.
- Register with `engine.New(...)` in `module.go` + `module.Register`.
- **Virtual models** (`virtual: true`): no Postgres table; declare fields for `{app}Views`, implement `engine.RegisterModel` List in Setup (before CQRS mounts). Example: appman.

## Views

Declare every screen under `views:`. Do not leave a menu `view:` to a discovered page only, and do not put `kind` / `columns` / `groups` on the view itself.

A screen is a list of `components` plus a `layout` tree. Each component has an `id` and is one collection or form. Catalog name is `{View}.{id}`.

```yaml
views:
  - name: GreetingList          # dynamic screen — no path; the shell renders layout
    layout: column             # shorthand: stack every component; or row
    components:
      - id: list
        kind: collection       # collection | table | kanban | chart | form
        model: greeting
        defaultView: table
        views: [table, kanban]
        groupBy: [mood]
        columns:
          - { field: message, width: 2fr, order: 1 }
          - { field: mood, order: 2 }
        filters:               # replaces the model's presets for this component
          - id: happy
            labelKey: hellospec.filter.happy
            domain:
              - [mood, "=", happy]
  - name: GreetingForm
    layout:                    # nested regions; span = track weight, size = track (1fr, 18rem, 40%, auto)
      direction: column
      items:
        - direction: row
          items:
            - { component: form, span: 2 }
            - { component: recent, span: 1, size: 18rem }
    components:
      - id: form
        kind: form
        model: greeting
        groups:
          - labelKey: hellospec.menu.group
            columns: 2
            fields:
              - { field: message, span: 2, widget: textarea, order: 1 }
              - { field: mood, span: 1, order: 2 }
      - id: recent
        kind: collection
        model: greeting
        columns:
          - { field: message, order: 1 }
  - name: GreetingBoard        # compiled page; .tsx only places the tree
    path: views/GreetingBoard.page.tsx
    layout:
      direction: column
      items:
        - { component: composer, size: auto }
        - { component: board, size: 1fr }
    components:
      - id: board
        kind: collection
        model: greeting
        columns:
          - { field: message, order: 1 }
  - name: Domains              # bespoke page — path only, no components
    path: views/Domains.page.tsx
```

Rules:

- One component: `layout: column` (or `row`) and a single `components` entry. `span` / `size` on that entry apply.
- Several components: a `layout` mapping. A node is either `component: <id>` or `direction` + `items`. Nest rows inside columns. `span` defaults to 1 (`Nfr`). `size` overrides the track (`1fr`, `2fr`, `18rem`, `40%`, `auto`).
- `path:` is a compiled `views/<Name>.page.tsx`. The page renders `<SpecLayout />` when it has a layout tree, or `<SpecScreen id="…" />` for one component. Do not hardcode columns, filters, or group-by in the `.tsx`.
- A page with no model screen (settings chrome, wizards) is `path` only.
- Do not set both top-level `kind` and `components`.
- Widgets: `input`, `textarea`, `checkbox`, `select`, `relation`. Any other `widget` id is a compiled `registerFieldWidget` component.
- Admins edit the same YAML with `domain set-view <app> <View>` (`-ted` in the web terminal).

List/form metadata from `{app}Views` drives `SpecScreen` / `KCollection` / `KForm`. After schema or view changes, components must expose `columns` or `fields` and the CQRS bindings for search and pagination.

## Keymap

```yaml
# app.yaml
keymap:
  - keymap.yaml
```

Bindings merge into `GET /api/keymap`. Shell/K chrome belongs in **core**; app-specific shortcuts use `scope: app` and `nav.<app>` / `custom:` / `element:` as needed. See `.cursor/rules/keymap.mdc`.

## Go

- Follow `packages/sdk-go` and `docs/internals/go-sdk.md`.
- Keep hooks next to models; list page args (`page`, `pageSize`, `domain`, `q`, `searchIn`, `groupBy`) already exist — do not reinvent.
